▸ Scheduled task: {{ name }}

{{ description }}

It came due at {{ due_at }}. Nobody asked for this just now — the clock did — and
that timestamp is the run's name: you say it back when you close the run.

**1. Start it as a background task, under exactly this name.**

    agent_task_start(name="{{ name }}", description="<the description above>")

It runs as you, on your own context, and the call returns at once. **Do not wait
for it, and do not poll it.**

**2. Close the run when its answer comes back.**

The answer arrives by itself, as a message on the `agent-task:{{ name }}` channel
wearing `[AsyncTaskResult:…]`. Nothing about it reaches this ledger on its own —
so when it arrives, close the run with what it produced:

    schedule_run_settle(name="{{ name }}", due_at="{{ due_at }}", note="<one line>")

The note is what this ledger keeps instead of the work: what you found, or what
you made, or where it went. Until you call that, the run stays `pending` — the one
state nobody can account for — and `schedule_runs` will show it as such.
